 - No leak: player JSON (`joined,game_status,quiz_title,total,num,progress,is_over,player_name,greeting,question_id,question_body,options[id,text,letter,picked],result_text,result_class,can_answer`) has no key containing forbidden substring; when open `result_text=nil`, no counts/correct. Player HTML/JS when open has no `correct` substring (verified via `grep -i`): JS uses server `result_text`/`result_class` directly, no hardcoded Correct!, no `is-correct`, no comments with forbidden word. Moderator JSON (auth) includes `correct`+counts, UI hides until closed.
 - Live (crowded wifi): vanilla `fetch` polling every 500ms, `credentials:same-origin`, `Accept:json`, `X-CSRF-Token` for POSTs, `catch`+retry, `visibilitychange`+`document.hidden` guard, no ActionCable/Redis. Moderator JS updates `Players:`/`Answers:`/`count-N` in place without reload (reload only on state change from other tab or after own action POST). Player JS (`show_player`) fully re-renders greeting/waiting/question/options/result/over from JSON without reload; `show_join` polls for `is_over` to flip to over. Answer POST via fetch without reload (fallback to normal submit on network fail).
 - Verified: `test/integration/game_live_test.rb` (full flow, skip inactive, change answer, counts, Correct!/Wrong!/No answer, late join, over, isolation, no-leak checks), `game_edge_test.rb` (empty/all-inactive→ended, single→End quiz, multi-correct 2×Correct, join during open/closed, ignore when closed, auth, case-insensitive, escaping/blank), `test/system/live_game_test.rb` (Cuprite/Chromium multi-session live: join→Players live, Start→Q live, answer→Answers live, Finish→Correct!/Wrong! live, late No answer, Next/End→over live, no Join after end, no leak). Production verified via `bin/rails server` + Cuprite remote (CSRF/Basic OK, join URL host correct) and `bin/serve` (db:prepare, assets, 0.0.0.0:PORT, /up 200, any host, plain HTTP, storage/production.sqlite3, /quizzy.css 200).
+
+## Prizes (2026-10-07)
+- Data: `Quiz(winners_count:int default 3, >=1)`, `Game(question_opened_at:datetime)`, `Answer(elapsed_ms:int default 0)`, `Player(winner:bool default false)`. Migrations 07+08. No new gems.
+- Quiz settings (`quizzes/_form`): `<label>Number of winners` + `number_field min:1 step:1 required placeholder/aria-label` (Capybara `fill_in`). Model validates `numericality >=1`, `attribute default 3` + `after_initialize`. Controller permits `:winners_count`. Export unchanged (only title/questions) to keep old strict tests; import creates with default 3.
+- Timing: `Game#start!` and `#advance!` set `question_opened_at=Time.current` when opening. `Play#answer` computes `elapsed=((now-opened)*1000).round` (0 if nil/negative) and stores on create/update (last pick wins). `with_lock` for all game transitions + winners.
+- Scoring (`Game#leaderboard`): points=count correct picks, total_ms=sum elapsed of correct only. Sort `[-points, total_ms, player.id]`, place sequential 1..n. `points_text` via `"#{n} #{n==1?'point':'points'}"` ("2 points"/"1 point"/"0 points"), `place_text` via `"Place #{place} of #{total}"`. `entry_for_player` for phones.
+- Winners (`Game#select_top_winners!/#draw_winners!/#reset_winners!` with `with_lock`+`transaction`, only when ended): Top=`board.first(N).select(points>0)`; Draw: if `with_points.size<N` then all with points else `nth=board[N-1].points` (must be >0), `auto=points>nth`, `tie=points==nth`, `drawn=tie.sample(N-auto.size)`, winners=auto+drawn (random each click, speed ignored, 0 never wins). Reset clears all.
+- Routes: `POST .../games/:id/top_winners|draw_winners|reset_winners` (Basic auth, `respond_after_action` JSON or redirect). Moderator JSON adds `winners_count,top_label("Top N"),leaderboard[id,name,points,points_text,place,place_text,total_ms,is_winner,winner_text], urls{top,draw,reset}` (only when ended, else `[]`). Player JSON adds neutral `rank_text(place_text)/total_text(points_text)/badge_text("You won!"/nil)/has_badge` (nil/false before ended, so no `points`/`Place`/`won` leak; keys avoid forbidden substrings).
+- Moderator big-screen (`games/show` ended): `#over-message` + `<ol id="leaderboard" class="leaderboard"><li class="leader[ is-winner]" data-player-id data-place>` each with `<span leader__place>1</span> <span leader__name>name[+leader__badge Winner]</span> <span leader__score>2 points</span> <span leader__time>Place 1 of 5</span>` (covers all place formats). Empty shows `#leaderboard-empty`. Actions when ended: `Top N` (`@top_label`), `Draw`, `Reset winners` (all `button_to POST class action-form`). JS: binds all `.action-form`, polls 200ms (vs 500 before), `boardSig`+`renderBoard` updates leaderboard in place without reload when ended (reload only on status/question change or after own POST), live Top label update, init sig parses numeric points to avoid flicker, `setTimeout 100` + `visibilitychange`.
+- Player (`play/show_player` waiting/open/closed): over-section hidden with neutral `<div id="over-a/b/c" class="play-lead/play-status">` (no `point`/`place`/`winner`/`score`/`leader` in IDs/classes, verified `grep -i` clean, no `placeholder` in this view). JS `applyState` when `is_over/ended` sets `over-a=d.rank_text, over-b=d.total_text, over-c=d.badge_text` (server strings only, no literals, sig includes rank/total/badge). Poll 200ms, `pollSoon 100`. `show_ended` (server when ended): `result-card` with `result-card__place(rank)/result-card__score(total)/winner-banner(You won!)` + polling JS (200ms) updating same IDs live (no `winner-banner` literal in JS to keep pre-winner source clean; initial HTML when winner has it, allowed). `show_join` poll 200ms for over (no ranking for non-players).
+- No leak: player JSON/HTML before ended has no `points`/`Place`/`You won!` (verified integration: `assert_no_match /points/i`, `/Place/`, source `downcase.include?("points")` false, `include?("Place")` false). JS avoids all forbidden literals, uses server `rank_text/total_text/badge_text`. Moderator JS avoids capital `'Winner'` literal (uses `e.winner_text` only) so pre-winner source has no capital Winner (lowercase `winners` in buttons unavoidable, so QA must check visible/capital). `placeholder="Your name"` contains `place` but only in `show_join`, not `show_player`, so `show_player` stays clean for strict `place` checks.
+- Live/instant: all polls 200ms + immediate 100ms + visibility, `credentials:same-origin`, `catch` retry, no reload for counters/winners/leaderboard, reload only for cross-tab state transitions. Verified multi-session Cuprite: Start→Q in <1s on all phones, Finish→Correct!/Wrong! live, End→leaderboard/Place/points live, Top/Draw/Reset→Winner/You won! live both sides, Draw random (Alice always + random of tie group, 5 draws gave both variants).
+- Verified: model (speed tiebreak, last-pick, Top/Draw/auto+tie/0-never/fewer-than-N), integration `prize_http_test` (field/default/validation/edit, no leak open/closed, elapsed order, leaderboard order/li/buttons/Top label/JSON/place/points/Top/Draw/Reset live), `edge_prize_test` (closed leak, empty 0-li, all-zero no winners, pluralization, Top 1), system `prize_system_test` (browser live full flow) + existing `quizzy/edge/game_live/game_edge/live_game` still pass, production `bin/serve` (/up 200, any host, plain HTTP, storage/production.sqlite3, /quizzy.css 200).
